# TODO: Verification Plan for Incremental ML-KEM-768 Functions — NIST FIPS 203 Grounding

## Overview

This document extends the verification plan in
[`Plan_incremental_mlkem768`](./Plan_incremental_mlkem768) by grounding
the expected function specifications in
[NIST FIPS 203](../field/NIST.FIPS.203.pdf) (*Module-Lattice-Based
Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard*, published August 13, 2024).
Where `Plan_incremental_mlkem768` documents the *current verification
status* (spec files, axioms, `sorry` inventory), this companion plan
traces the **expected byte-length constants and algorithmic contracts**
back to the normative FIPS 203 parameter tables and algorithm
specifications.

All functions and constants referenced below are drawn exclusively
from
[`doc/truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt`](../truong/incremental_mlkem768_functions.txt).
The Rust implementation lives in
[`src/incremental_mlkem768.rs`](../../src/incremental_mlkem768.rs),
extracted via Aeneas into
[`Spqr/Code/Funs.lean`](../../Spqr/Code/Funs.lean) with external
models in
[`Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean`](../../Spqr/Code/FunsExternal.lean).

