### 5b. What FIPS 203 Properties Are NOT Verified

The following FIPS 203 properties are **outside the verification
scope** because the upstream `libcrux_ml_kem` functions are treated
as opaque:

| Property | FIPS 203 Source | Why Not Verified |
|----------|----------------|-----------------|
| Correctness: K' = K with probability ≥ 1 − 2⁻¹⁶⁴·⁸ | §3.2, Table 1 | `decapsulate_compressed_key` is opaque; returns `default` |
| IND-CCA2 security | §3.2 | Computational security property; not expressible as a Lean type-level theorem |
| Modulus check: ByteEncode₁₂(ByteDecode₁₂(ek[0:384k])) == ek[0:384k] | §7.2, Eq. 7.1 | `validate_pk_bytes` is opaque; trivialised to always-Ok |
| NTT correctness: NTT⁻¹(NTT(f)) = f | §4.3, Algs. 9–10 | Internal to opaque libcrux functions |
| Compression/decompression round-trip | §4.2.1, Eqs. 4.7–4.8 | Internal to opaque libcrux functions |
| CBD sampling distribution: coefficients in {−η, …, η} | §4.2.2, Alg. 8 | Used only in η₂ detection logic (F6, opaque) |
