### 5c. Implicit Rejection (FIPS 203 §6.3, Alg. 18 lines 6–11)

FIPS 203 specifies that ML-KEM.Decaps_internal performs an
"implicit rejection" when the re-encrypted ciphertext c' does not
match the input ciphertext c (Alg. 18, lines 9–11). In this case,
the output K' is replaced with K̄ = J(z‖c), a pseudorandom value
derived from the decapsulation key's random component z and the
ciphertext c.

This behaviour is entirely internal to the opaque
`decapsulate_compressed_key` function and is not modelled in the
extraction (which returns `default`). The verification therefore does
**not** prove that implicit rejection is correctly implemented.

