### 6d. Composite Spec Theorem Sketch: Full KEM Round-Trip

Composing the individual spec theorems along the FIPS 203 chain, one
obtains the following composite property (stated informally — not yet
a Lean theorem):

```
-- Informal composite spec (not yet in Lean)
theorem kem_round_trip_sizes
    {R : Type} (rngInst : rand.rng.Rng R)
    (cryptoRngInst : rand_core.CryptoRng R) (rng : R)
    (hfb : fill_bytes_ok rngInst.rand_coreRngCoreInst)
    (hpfs : potentially_fix_state_ok)
    (har : option_as_ref_id) :
    -- Step 1: KeyGen (FIPS 203 Alg. 19)
    generate rngInst cryptoRngInst rng ⦃ (keys_rng : Keys × R) =>
      let keys := keys_rng.1
      let rng1 := keys_rng.2
      -- keys.hdr.length = 64  ∧  keys.ek.length = 1152  ∧  keys.dk.length = 2400
      -- Step 2: Key validation (FIPS 203 §7.2)
      ek_matches_header keys.ek keys.hdr ⦃ (valid : Bool) =>
        valid = true ∧
        -- Step 3: Encaps phase 1 (FIPS 203 Alg. 20, first half)
        encaps1 rngInst cryptoRngInst keys.hdr rng1 ⦃ (enc1_rng : _ × R) =>
          let (ct1, es, ss) := enc1_rng.1
          -- ct1.length = 960  ∧  es.length = 2080  ∧  ss.length = 32
          -- Step 4: Encaps phase 2 (FIPS 203 Alg. 20, second half)
